<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58020" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῠδων-ίζω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>:—elsewh. in 
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be buffeted,
				swept by heavy seas</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν κυβερνήτην
				-ίζεσθαι καὶ ἀστοχεῖν θαλασσομαχοῦντα</span> Vett. Val.
				<i><span class="en">
				354.26
			</span></i>; -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ομένη ναῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phlp.
					<u>in APo.</u>
					381.7
				</span></i>
			: usu. metaph., <i>to be disturbed, thrown into
			confusion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἄδικοι κλυδωνισθήσονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Is.</u>
					57.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμος ταρασσόμενος καὶ -ιζόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					9.11.3
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be tossed about</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντὶ ἀνέμῳ τῆς διδασκαλίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Eph.</u>
					4.14
				</span></i>
			.</div>
